  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Seasonal and mostly dry weather is expected through \nSaturday.\n\nA surface high will build across the eastern Great Lakes tonight. \nCool northwest flow aloft will continue to support some lake effect \nand upslope clouds, but dry weather is expected. Lows will drop back \ninto the 30s in most areas, with some 20s across the North Country.\n\nHigh pressure will crest over the eastern Great Lakes Saturday, with \ndry weather, a return to sunshine, and near average temperatures. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A warming trend is expected Sunday through early \nnext week.\n\nSurface high pressure will move east of the region Saturday night. A \nsoutherly flow will support warmer weather Sunday with highs back in \nthe low 60s. High pressure will move off the east coast early next \nweek, while the westward extent remains across the Northeast. This \nwill support a warm, and dry period through at least Tuesday. \n\nA deep trough is expected to move from the Plains to the Mississippi \nValley by mid-week. There remains high uncertainty in the evolution \nof a surface low and how quick moisture returns to the eastern Great \nLakes region. Chances for showers begin to increase Wednesday with \nthe potential for unsettled weather to continue through the end of \nthe work week. Above normal temperatures are expected mid to \nlate week.",
